ss; within a namespace, the default store is\n  shared by that namespace's playground OGXServer instances.\n- Keep the OGXServer application storage configuration on its existing default — this change\n  touches only the vector_io provider configuration (no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL application\n  storage migration).\n- Ensure no additional manual setup steps appear in the user path from zero to a working RAG\n  playground, compared to the current experience.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- When a playground with RAG is configured, the gen-ai BFF creates/configures the OGXServer\n  instance with the remote pgvector vector_io provider enabled.\n- PostgreSQL connection details are consumed from a namespaced reference (not hardcoded), and\n  the design allows swapping the connection source to the platform-provided shared database\n  without changing the wiring logic.\n- Per-namespace isolation is enforced: playgrounds in different namespaces use separate\n  default vector stores, and no cross-namespace vector data access is possible.\n- A user reaches a working RAG playground without manually provisioning or configuring\n  external infrastructure.\n- The OGXServer application storage configuration remains on its existing default after this\n  change.\n- The wired configuration is demonstrated to work against a pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL\n  instance available in the namespace (regardless of which mechanism provisioned it).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI\n  without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\" (user\n  path portion).\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the\n  default vector store with no loss of current capability\" (wiring portion).\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for\n  multi-tenant environments (e.g., per-namespace isolation)\".\n- Staff Engineer Input: vector_io provider configuration is separate from application storage\n  backend configuration; per-namespace scoping preferred; portability toward the RHOAI 3.6\n  platform-provided shared PostgreSQL.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59047,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b24000d35afb1c95","agent_id":"a2f51b2238c42403f","session_id":"d17e1aa1-c63c-47fc-8da1-f24a565f8f93","uuid":"da970d31-4993-4fe5-ac72-f32d093eb105","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:34:55.566Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
