ual setup steps for RAG workflows\n  compared to the current experience.\n- Execute the validation against an environment where the default vector store is deployed via\n  the provisioning mechanism selected by the go/no-go decision.\n- Document the limitations of the default store: it is for development experimentation, and\n  users with production-scale vector workloads should use an external vector database.\n- Fix defects surfaced by the validation in the wiring or provider integration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A validation report demonstrates playground RAG workflows (ingestion, retrieval, RAG chat)\n  functioning with the default vector store with no loss of current capability versus the\n  inline-provider experience.\n- A benchmark report captures the inline Milvus baseline and the pgvector measurements on\n  representative playground RAG workloads and shows pgvector within the same order of\n  magnitude.\n- A resource sizing recommendation for the provisioned PostgreSQL instance is produced,\n  derived from the model-registry-operator reference sizing and the benchmark results.\n- The validation is executed against an environment where the default vector store is deployed\n  via the provisioning mechanism selected by the go/no-go decision.\n- The out-of-the-box experience is verified: no additional manual setup steps are required for\n  RAG workflows compared to the current experience.\n- The default store's intended scope (development experimentation; external vector database\n  for production-scale workloads) is documented.\n- All defects found during validation in the vector_io wiring or provider integration are\n  fixed and re-validated.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the\n  default vector store with no loss of current capability\" (validation portion).\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in\n  resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead\" (benchmark +\n  sizing).\n- Strategy success criteria \"no functional regression\" and \"no additional manual setup steps\".\n- Staff Engineer Input: performance and index thresholds are development-experimentation\n  scope (order-of-magnitude benchmark, flat scan sufficient); PostgreSQL resource sizing\n  referenced from model-registry-operator and adjusted after benchmarking.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":60002,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b24000d35afb1c95","agent_id":"a2f51b2238c42403f","session_id":"d17e1aa1-c63c-47fc-8da1-f24a565f8f93","uuid":"9f31ca10-f77f-42f6-96b8-7f08e3f2dd7e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:35:11.983Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
