{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b063e665-2619-4e18-a116-6a612b084935","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8841978427b0eec0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-0adeup6k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E005.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store\n\n## Description\n\nBranch A of the provisioning-mechanism decision: the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered\nby the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands in time for RHOAI 3.5, and\nthis epic implements PostgreSQL lifecycle management for the Gen AI Studio default vector\nstore in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's self-provisioning\npattern. For each namespace where a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG requires it, the\noperator provisions a PostgreSQL 16 instance with pgvector using the existing Red Hat image —\nno custom image build and no Konflux onboarding are needed, because\n`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` already includes pgvector and the\n`RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` reference is already wired in the rhods-operator CSV for\ndisconnected installs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement per-namespace PostgreSQL (pgvector) provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator\n  layer for Gen AI Studio, following the model-registry-operator pattern: Deployment, Service,\n  persistent storage, and a credentials Secret reconciled from the operator.\n- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) as the provisioned\n  database image; wire the image reference for disconnected installs through the existing\n  `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` mechanism.\n- Set the provisioned instance's resource requests/limits starting from the\n  model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing.\n- Implement lifecycle management via the operator's reconciliation loop: provisioning when a\n  playground with RAG needs a default vector store in the namespace, and cleanup when the\n  playground/namespace no longer requires it; credential rotation handled through\n  reconciliation.\n- Expose the provisioned instance's connection details as a namespaced reference that the\n  gen-ai BFF's OGXServer wiring consumes.\n- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL becomes available\n  (RHOAI 3.6), the consuming wiring can switch to the shared connection string instead of the\n  operator-provisioned instance.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The operator layer provisions a PostgreSQL 16 instance with pgvector in each namespace where\n  a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG requires a default vector store, following the\n  model-registry-operator provisioning pattern (Deployment, Service, persistent storage,\n  credentials Secret).\n- The provisioned instance uses `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` with no custom image\n  build, and the image reference resolves in disconnected installs via the existing\n  `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` mechanism.\n- Resource requests/limits for the provisioned instance start from the model-registry\n  operator's PostgreSQL sizing.\n- Lifecycle is managed by reconciliation: the instance is removed when the playground or\n  namespace no longer requires it, and credential rotation is supported.\n- The provisioned instance's connection details are available as a namespaced reference\n  consumable by the playground OGXServer wiring.\n- No Konflux onboarding, repo onboarding, or custom image build is introduced by this epic.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI\n  without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\"\n  (provisioning portion, branch A).\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store runs as a separate process,\n  decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider)\" (separately provisioned\n  PostgreSQL instance).\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for\n  multi-tenant environments (e.g., per-namespace isolation)\" (per-namespace provisioning).\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in\n  resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead\" (reference\n  resource sizing).\n- Staff Engineer Input: self-provisioning via the model-registry-operator pattern in the\n  operator layer from RHAISTRAT-7164; Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image with pgvector already\n  exists; resource sizing referenced from model-registry-operator.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":60936,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b24000d35afb1c95","agent_id":"a2f51b2238c42403f","session_id":"d17e1aa1-c63c-47fc-8da1-f24a565f8f93","uuid":"e428bc14-9bfe-4e1b-95b9-7a61edbe53cd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:35:28.460Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
