{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb517fb014450228","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tepic_count: 6\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8004: Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio\n11\t\n12\t## Source Material and Staff Engineer Input Precedence\n13\t\n14\tThe full strategy body (attachment `RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`) was not provisioned in this\n15\tworkspace; the decomposition is derived from the strategy summary, acceptance criteria, open\n16\tquestions, and the **Staff Engineer Input** section, which per the decomposition rules takes\n17\tprecedence over the AI-generated technical approach. Every Staff Engineer override is logged\n18\tbelow (see Staff Engineer Input Overrides). Where the AI-generated strategy and the Staff\n19\tEngineer Input diverge, the Staff Engineer Input was followed.\n20\t\n21\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides\n22\t\n23\t| # | Override | Effect on decomposition |\n24\t|---|----------|------------------------|\n25\t| 1 | OGX does **not** auto-provision PostgreSQL — OGX defaults to SQLite; the gen-ai BFF hardcodes SQLite for OGXServer instances. Introducing PostgreSQL is new work, not an extension of existing infrastructure | The provisioning work (branch epics) is modeled as genuinely new implementation, not configuration |\n26\t| 2 | A Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image with pgvector already exists (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`); `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` is already in the rhods-operator CSV; model-registry-operator already uses this pattern | **No custom image build epic, no Konflux onboarding epic, no repo-onboarding epic, and no rhods-operator epic** — the strategy's 1-2 sprint image onboarding estimate is eliminated |\n27\t| 3 | Platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC arrives in RHOAI 3.6; for 3.5 Gen AI Studio must provision its own PostgreSQL instance | Self-provisioning is the committed 3.5 scope; portability to the 3.6 shared database is an acceptance criterion on the wiring and provisioning epics |\n28\t| 4 | Self-provisioning via the model-registry-operator pattern requires a RHOAI-controlled operator (RHAISTRAT-7164, dashboard operator modularization, In Progress) — a hard dependency; go/no-go gate to be defined in sprint planning | Investigation epic E001 (go/no-go) with two conditional branches for the provisioning mechanism |\n29\t| 5 | Fallbacks if RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land: BFF-managed provisioning (guardrails-style), or last resort bring-your-own PostgreSQL | Branch B epic; BYO documented as the gate's last-resort fallback rather than an epic |\n30\t| 6 | **Decouple from Auto Rag** — Auto Rag integration targets RHOAI 3.6 via RHAISTRAT-7824; remove Auto Rag from affected components, impacted teams, acceptance criteria, and validation | Auto Rag removed from all epic scope; strategy AC-3 is not covered by any epic (see HLR Traceability Matrix) |\n31\t| 7 | Performance scope: no strict latency SLAs; sprint-1 benchmark captures the inline Milvus baseline and verifies pgvector is the same order of magnitude; flat scan (no index) is sufficient; latency/corpus/index-type open questions removed | Validation epic E004 uses order-of-magnitude benchmark ACs, not threshold SLAs |\n32\t| 8 | PostgreSQL resource sizing: start from model-registry-operator's requests/limits, adjust after benchmarking | Sizing ACs on branch epics (reference) and E004 (adjustment) |\n33\t| 9 | Existing remote vector store implementation is largely reusable; the majority of effort is PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning, not the vector_io provider integration | Small provider epic (E002, OGX Core) + larger provisioning branch epics |\n34\t| 10 | Vector storage and application storage are independent configurations — only the pgvector vector_io provider (`remote::pgvector` via `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`) is configured; application storage stays on SQLite; no SQLite→PostgreSQL migration concern | No migration/consolidation epic; \"application storage unchanged\" is an AC on E002 and E003 |\n35\t\n36\t## Epic List\n37\t\n38\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n39\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n40\t| E001 | Go/no-go decision: PostgreSQL provisioning mechanism for the Gen AI Studio default vector store | Investigation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n41\t| E002 | Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution | Implementation | OGX Core | OGX Core | P0 |\n42\t| E003 | Wire Gen AI Studio playground OGXServer instances to the remote pgvector vector store | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n43\t| E004 | Validate Gen AI Studio playground RAG on the default pgvector vector store (capability parity, benchmark, sizing) | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n44\t| BRANCH-A-E005 | Operator-based PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store (branch A: RHAISTRAT-7164 lands in time) | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n45\t| BRANCH-B-E005 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds (branch B: RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land in time) | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n46\t\n47\tBranch epics are conditional alternatives selected by the E001 investigation outcome; they are\n48\tattached to E001 as a plan document, not created as standalone Jira issues.\n49\t\n50\t## Dependency DAG\n51\t\n52\t```mermaid\n53\tgraph TD\n54\t    E001[\"E001 Go/no-go: provisioning mechanism (Investigation)\"]\n55\t    E002[\"E002 OGX remote pgvector vector_io provider\"]\n56\t    E003[\"E003 Playground OGXServer pgvector wiring\"]\n57\t    E004[\"E004 Validation: parity, benchmark, sizing\"]\n58\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E005 Operator-based PostgreSQL provisioning\"]\n59\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E00