(`RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`) referenced by the Jira description was not provisioned, so\n129\t   the Affected Components table, Impacted Teams table, numbered HLR list, dependencies table,\n130\t   and NFRs were unavailable. Team assignments were derived from component ownership\n131\t   (Gen AI Studio work → Gen AI Studio team; ogx-distribution work → OGX Core team); component\n132\t   names were matched to canonical RHAI components. Verify team assignments against the full\n133\t   strategy when available.\n134\t2. **Schedule risk — hard external dependency:** RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator\n135\t   modularization, In Progress) gates the preferred operator-based provisioning branch. Per the\n136\t   Staff Engineer Input it will be challenging to commit this strategy to a specific release\n137\t   until that dependency is delivered. The go/no-go gate (E001) manages this; the BFF-managed\n138\t   branch and the BYO fallback bound the worst case.\n139\t3. **Open question resolved by direction, not decision:** the scoping-model open question\n140\t   (per-namespace vs. per-instance) is treated as resolved toward per-namespace because the\n141\t   Staff Engineer Input removes Auto Rag (the per-instance driver) from scope and the fallback\n142\t   provisioning description is per-namespace. The implementing team should confirm per-namespace\n143\t   scoping at E001's decision point.\n144\t4. **Deferred open question — migration path:** whether users need a migration path from the\n145\t   default vector store to a production-grade vector database is not resolved by the Staff\n146\t   Engineer Input. The pgvector choice itself aligns with commonly-used vector database\n147\t   providers (Staff Engineer framing), and the validation epic documents that the default store\n148\t   is for development experimentation. A future migration-path work item should be raised\n149\t   separately if product decides it is needed.\n150\t5. **Priority load:** the strategy is a Blocke