{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-833f837ff5c2fec5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: OGX Core\n6\tteam: OGX Core\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the OGX-distribution side of the default vector store: the remote pgvector\n34\tvector_io provider (`remote::pgvector`, activated via the `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` environment guard)\n35\tis available, correctly configured, and validated in the OGX distribution so that RAG vector\n36\tstorage runs against a separate PostgreSQL process instead of the inline Milvus provider\n37\tbundled in the Llama Stack process. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector\n38\tstore implementation is largely reusable — this is the smaller share of the strategy's effort —\n39\tand only the vector_io provider configuration changes: the OGX application storage backend\n40\t(key-value and SQL stores) is an independent configuration and remains on its existing SQLite\n41\tdefault. No SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is in scope because application storage is not\n42\ttouched.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Verify and, where needed, adjust the OGX distribution build and runtime configuration so the\n47\t  remote pgvector vector_io provider can be activated through its environment guard for RHOAI\n48\t  deployments.\n49\t- Reuse the existing remote vector store implementation for the pgvector integration; extend\n50\t  only where pgvector-specific gaps are found.\n51\t- Validate that the provider operates decoupled from the OGX server process: the vector store\n52\t  is a separate PostgreSQL instance reached over the network, not an inline provider running\n53\t  inside the OGX process.\n54\t- Confirm the distribution remains shippable without the inline vector providers (the\n55\t  distribution already strips inline providers such as milvus-inline from its build\n56\t  configuration).\n57\t- Confirm the provider works against the Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image that includes pgvector\n58\t  out of the box (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`) — no custom image build.\n59\t- Leave the OGX application storage configuration (key-value and SQL backends) unchanged.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- The remote pgvector vector_io provider can be activated in the OGX distribution\n64\t  configuration via its environment guard against a PostgreSQL 16 instance with the pgvector\n65\t  extension enabled.\n66\t- Vector insert and similarity-search round trips succeed through the distribution's vector\n67\t  I/O API against the remote pgvector instance.\n68\t- The RAG vector store used with the provider runs as a separate process from the OGX server\n69\t  (no inline vector provider in the serving path).\n70\t- The provider is validated against `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` with no custom\n71\t  container image build introduced.\n72\t- The OGX application storage configuration is unchanged from its existing default (vector\n73\t  storage and application storage remain independent configurations).\n74\t- The distribution's build configuration still excludes inline vector providers.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store runs as a separate process,\n79\t  decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider)\".\n80\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the\n81\t  default vector store with no loss of current capability\" (provider integration portion).\n82\t- Staff Engineer Input: \"Existing remote vector store implementation is reusable\" and\n83\t  \"Vector storage and application storage are independent configurations\" (vector_io provider\n84\t  only; application storage untouched).\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b90007d49630d841","agent_id":"af41092d649637995","session_id":"d17e1aa1-c63c-47fc-8da1-f24a565f8f93","uuid":"b8cc3dbf-7b27-4cd9-997f-da3a3f94903d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:37:44.545Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-833f837ff5c2fec5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
