{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a94654e41402ceb0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E004\n3\ttitle: Validate Gen AI Studio playground RAG on the default pgvector vector store\n4\t  (capability parity, benchmark, sizing)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n14\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: rewrite\n17\t  fallback_approach: If neither self-provisioning mechanism is viable and the bring-your-own-PostgreSQL\n18\t    last resort is invoked, the validation is rewritten to validate the documented\n19\t    manual configuration path and its user-facing impact instead of an out-of-the-box\n20\t    default vector store.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: 1\n27\t  external_dependency: 1\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 7\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\tbranch: null\n37\t---\n38\t# Validate Gen AI Studio playground RAG on the default pgvector vector store (capability parity, benchmark, sizing)\n39\t\n40\t## Description\n41\t\n42\tThis epic delivers the end-to-end validation evidence that the default pgvector vector store\n43\tpreserves the out-of-the-box Gen AI Studio playground RAG experience now that the inline\n44\tprovider is going away: functional capability-parity validation, an order-of-magnitude\n45\tperformance comparison against the inline Milvus baseline, and a resource sizing\n46\trecommendation for the provisioned PostgreSQL instance. The default store is intended for\n47\tdevelopment experimentation, not production usage — strict latency SLAs are explicitly not\n48\trequired; the benchmark verifies pgvector is in the same order of magnitude as the inline\n49\tMilvus baseline on typical playground RAG workloads (small document sets, flat scan).\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Validate playground RAG workflows end to end with the default vector store: document-set\n54\t  ingestion, retrieval, and RAG chat, compared against the current inline-provider experience\n55\t  for loss of capability.\n56\t- Capture the inline Milvus baseline benchmark and the corresponding pgvector measurements on\n57\t  representative playground RAG workloads; verify same-order-of-magnitude performance (no\n58\t  threshold SLAs; typical usage involves small document sets where flat scan is sufficient).\n59\t- Produce a resource sizing recommendation for the provisioned PostgreSQL instance, starting\n60\t  from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource requests/limits and adjusted based on\n61\t  the benchmark results.\n62\t- Verify the out-of-the-box experience: no additional manual setup steps for RAG workflows\n63\t  compared to the current experience.\n64\t- Execute the validation against an environment where the default vector store is deployed via\n65\t  the provisioning mechanism selected by the go/no-go decision.\n66\t- Document the limitations of the default store: it is for development experimentation, and\n67\t  users with production-scale vector workloads should use an external vector database.\n68\t- Fix defects surfaced by the validation in the wiring or provider integration.\n69\t\n70\t## Acceptance Criteria\n71\t\n72\t- A validation report demonstrates playground RAG workflows (ingestion, retrieval, RAG chat)\n73\t  functioning with the default vector store with no loss of current capability versus the\n74\t  inline-provider experience.\n75\t- A benchmark report captures the inline Milvus baseline and the pgvector measurements on\n76\t  representative playground RAG workloads and shows pgvector within the same order of\n77\t  magnitude.\n78\t- A resource sizing recommendation for the provisioned PostgreSQL instance is produced,\n79\t  derived from the model-registry-operator reference sizing and the benchmark results.\n80\t- The validation is executed against an environment where the default vector store is deployed\n81\t  via the provisioning mechanism selected by the go/no-go decision.\n82\t- The out-of-the-box experience is verified: no additional manual setup steps are required for\n83\t  RAG workflows compared to the current experience.\n84\t- The default store's intended scope (development experimentation; external vector database\n85\t  for production-scale workloads) is documented.\n86\t- All defects found during validation in the vector_io wiring or provider integration are\n87\t  fixed and re-validated.\n88\t\n89\t## HLR Traceability\n90\t\n91\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the\n92\t  default vector store with no loss of current capability\" (validation portion).\n93\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in\n94\t  resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead\" (benchmark +\n95\t  sizing).\n96\t- Strategy success criteria \"no functional regression\" and \"no additional manual setup steps\".\n97\t- Staff Engineer Input: performance and index thresholds are development-experimentation\n98\t  scope (order-of-magnitude benchmark, flat scan sufficient); PostgreSQL resource sizing\n99\t  referenced from model-registry-operator and adjusted after benchmarking.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b90007d49630d841","agent_id":"af41092d649637995","session_id":"d17e1aa1-c63c-47fc-8da1-f24a565f8f93","uuid":"720a0003-f9fb-49e7-abc9-0f1a5ad1c234","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:37:46.001Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a94654e41402ceb0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
