ff Engineer Input directs \"Remove Auto Rag from affected components,\n43\timpacted teams, acceptance criteria, and validation requirements,\" deferring it to\n44\tRHAISTRAT-7824 (RHOAI 3.6) — recorded in the matrix as a scope reduction, not an orphan.\n45\tAll epics are P0, matching the strategy's Blocker priority; no priority inheritance\n46\tviolations (the gating Investigation E001 is P0). No priority collapse — no epic bundles\n47\tdeferrable lower-priority HLRs.\n48\t\n49\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n50\tDiagram/frontmatter cross-check: every edge in the mermaid diagram (E002→E003,\n51\tE002→E004, E003→E004, E001→E004, E001⇢BRANCH-A-E005, E001⇢BRANCH-B-E005) has a matching\n52\tentry in the target epic's `dependencies`, and vice versa; arrows run dependency →\n53\tdependent as the convention requires. No circular dependencies, no edges to nonexistent\n54\tepics. Both branch files set `branch` (A/B, matching filenames) and `gated_by:\n55\tRHAISTRAT-8004-E001`, and E001 appears in their direct `dependencies`. No main-plan epic\n56\tlists a branch epic in its dependencies — E004 correctly depends on the Investigation\n57\tE001 itself rather than a branch node, which is the rule-compliant shape given the\n58\tbranches are attached to E001 as plan documents. No konflux-onboarding,\n59\tlicense-validation, or repo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is\n60\ttrivially satisfied; the Staff Engineer Correction 2 justification for omitting the\n61\tonboarding chain is sound and corroborated by the architecture context\n62\t(model-registry-operator's existing PostgreSQL provisioning, `RELATED_IMAGE` wiring).\n63\tCross-check of epic content for uncaptured data dependencies: the PostgreSQL connection\n64\treference consumed by E003 and the provisioned instance consumed by E004 are\n65\tconfiguration references / runtime content, correctly expressed as AC gates (E003's\n66\t\"available in the namespace regardless of which mechanism provisioned it\" AC; E004