on-edges table justifies.\n94\t\n95\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n96\tSignal sets are type-correct: E001 carries `investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric);\n97\tall five Implementation epics carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric); no cross-assignment.\n98\tE001's signals match its content: concrete bounded question (+1), answer not yet written\n99\tanywhere (0), no runtime experiment (0), no cluster dependence (0), and a decision the\n100\tStaff Engineer explicitly assigns to human sprint planning (-2). Implementation signal\n101\tvalues are consistent with their rationales and the strategy: BRANCH-A's\n102\texisting_foundation 0 / external_dependency -1 (operator layer not yet present, hard\n103\tRHAISTRAT-7164 dependency), BRANCH-B's open_questions -1 (unresolved lifecycle design),\n104\tE004's adapter_pattern 0 (validation work). architecture_claims is scored +1 on all\n105\tImplementation epics with architecture-context citations; spot-checks against\n106\t`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/` confirm the cited claims\n107\t(PGVector as a supported remote vector backend and milvus-inline stripped in\n108\togx-distribution.md; gen-ai BFF structure in odh-dashboard.md; the\n109\tmodel-registry-operator PostgreSQL provisioning pattern) — no calibration misses. One\n110\tminor nit: the rationale citations omit the `architecture/` path segment (cited as\n111\t`.context/architecture-context/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/...`); the files are identifiable and the\n112\tcited content is accurate, so this does not affect scoring.\n113\t\n114\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n115\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy and Staff Engineer directives.\n116\tRule-mandated AC check: no replacement epics (no konflux chain, no image build), so\n117\trollback/feature-flag and build-pipeline-green ACs are not applicable — correctly\n118\tomitted with explicit \"no custom image build / no Konflux onboarding\" ACs on the branch\n119\tepics instead. No docs-authoring epic exists, and none is required: the strategy file\n120\tcontains no Prerequisites & Process Gates / Documentation Support requirement, and the\n121\tsummary records the rationale (limitation notes as an incidental AC of E004). Soft-AC\n122\tscan: E001's \"reviewed and accepted in Gen AI Studio sprint planning\" AC was examined\n123\tand is valid — the reviewed decision record is the epic's own deliverable, and the Staff\n124\tEngineer Input explicitly directs the gate be defined in sprint planning; it is not an\n125\texternally-granted availability precondition. E004's environment AC is a condition on\n126\twhat the epic verifies, with scheduling handled by gated_by. No epic body references\n127\tsibling epics by draft ID — cross-epic references use real Jira keys (RHAISTRAT-7164)\n128\tor descriptive phrases (\"the go/no-go decision\").\n129\t\n130\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n131\tAll in-scope strategy scope is covered: out-of-the-box default store (branches + E003),\n132\tplayground RAG parity (E002/E003/E004), separate-process requirement (E002 + branches),\n133\tper-namespace scoping (E003 + branches), lightweight/resource sizing (E004 + branches),\n134\tand all three success criteria. Both strategy open questions are accounted for: the\n135\tscoping model is resolved into E001's decision record (with the per-namespace reasoning\n136\trecorded in Health Warning 3), and the migration-path question is explicitly deferred in\n137\tHealth Warning 4 rather than silently dropped. All ten Staff Engineer directives are\n138\ttraced through the override table to epic scope/ACs, including the corrections (SQLite\n139\tdefault, existing pgvector image, independent storage configurations). Conditional\n140\tbranches cover all bounded outcomes: branch A, branch B, and the bring-your-own\n141\tlast resort documented as the gate's fallback with its user-facing impact. The\n142\tRHAISTRAT-7164 schedule risk and the dev-experimentation performance scope are carried\n143\tforward into the relevant epics (E001, E004) and Health Warnings.\n144\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f5b4f1522ec11d6","agent_id":"a60c9d1c0958b41c0","session_id":"d17e1aa1-c63c-47fc-8da1-f24a565f8f93","uuid":"322bc9b1-cae7-42cf-ade0-f596efc55be7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:41:46.662Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8de247a15bfcb809","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 epics"}
