{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b612c43a14b20d8c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Wire Gen AI Studio playground OGXServer instances to the remote pgvector vector\n4\t  store\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 8\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Wire Gen AI Studio playground OGXServer instances to the remote pgvector vector store\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the Gen AI Studio side of the default vector store: the gen-ai BFF\n36\tconfigures the OGXServer instances it creates for the playground so that playground RAG\n37\tworkflows use the remote pgvector vector_io provider backed by the default PostgreSQL instance\n38\tprovisioned in the namespace, instead of relying on the inline provider bundled in the Llama\n39\tStack distribution. Users must get a working RAG playground out of the box — no manual\n40\tprovisioning or configuration of external infrastructure. The wiring is deliberately\n41\tmechanism-agnostic: the BFF consumes the PostgreSQL connection details from a reference in the\n42\tnamespace, so the same wiring works whether the instance is provisioned by the operator layer\n43\tor by the BFF itself, and can later point at the platform-provided shared database expected in\n44\tRHOAI 3.6 without redesign.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance-creation logic (the code path that today\n49\t  configures storage defaults when creating playground OGXServer instances) to enable the\n50\t  remote pgvector vector_io provider for playgrounds with RAG.\n51\t- Source the PostgreSQL connection details from a namespaced secret/reference rather than\n52\t  hardcoding them, so the producing side (operator-provisioned or BFF-provisioned instance\n53\t  now; platform-shared database in RHOAI 3.6) can change without reworking this wiring.\n54\t- Enforce per-namespace scoping: playgrounds in different namespaces use separate default\n55\t  vector stores with no cross-namespace data access; within a namespace, the default store is\n56\t  shared by that namespace's playground OGXServer instances.\n57\t- Keep the OGXServer application storage configuration on its existing default — this change\n58\t  touches only the vector_io provider configuration (no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL application\n59\t  storage migration).\n60\t- Ensure no additional manual setup steps appear in the user path from zero to a working RAG\n61\t  playground, compared to the current experience.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- When a playground with RAG is configured, the gen-ai BFF creates/configures the OGXServer\n66\t  instance with the remote pgvector vector_io provider enabled.\n67\t- PostgreSQL connection details are consumed from a namespaced reference (not hardcoded), and\n68\t  the design allows swapping the connection source to the platform-provided shared database\n69\t  without changing the wiring logic.\n70\t- Per-namespace isolation is enforced: playgrounds in different namespaces use separate\n71\t  default vector stores, and no cross-namespace vector data access is possible.\n72\t- A user reaches a working RAG playground without manually provisioning or configuring\n73\t  external infrastructure.\n74\t- The OGXServer application storage configuration remains on its existing default after this\n75\t  change.\n76\t- The wired configuration is demonstrated to work against a pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL\n77\t  instance available in the namespace (regardless of which mechanism provisioned it).\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI\n82\t  without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\" (user\n83\t  path portion).\n84\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the\n85\t  default vector store with no loss of current capability\" (wiring portion).\n86\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for\n87\t  multi-tenant environments (e.g., per-namespace isolation)\".\n88\t- Staff Engineer Input: vector_io provider configuration is separate from application storage\n89\t  backend configuration; per-namespace scoping preferred; portability toward the RHOAI 3.6\n90\t  platform-provided shared PostgreSQL.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d7bb69f15af0e6e","agent_id":"a967f2b83c82d8c30","session_id":"d17e1aa1-c63c-47fc-8da1-f24a565f8f93","uuid":"3bc8f8ce-1983-4289-9441-4d46228d3b20","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:43:03.376Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b612c43a14b20d8c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004"}
