{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94667ff5b8b7f5bd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E005\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector\n4\t  store\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n17\t    not deliver the RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for RHOAI 3.5, this branch\n18\t    is dropped and provisioning moves to the BFF-managed approach (guardrails-style\n19\t    provisioning by the gen-ai BFF), or to the bring-your-own-PostgreSQL last resort\n20\t    if neither is viable.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 0\n26\t  open_questions: 1\n27\t  external_dependency: -1\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 5\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL provisioning for the Gen AI Studio default vector store\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tBranch A of the provisioning-mechanism decision: the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered\n42\tby the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands in time for RHOAI 3.5, and\n43\tthis epic implements PostgreSQL lifecycle management for the Gen AI Studio default vector\n44\tstore in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's self-provisioning\n45\tpattern. For each namespace where a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG requires it, the\n46\toperator provisions a PostgreSQL 16 instance with pgvector using the existing Red Hat image —\n47\tno custom image build and no Konflux onboarding are needed, because\n48\t`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` already includes pgvector and the\n49\t`RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` reference is already wired in the rhods-operator CSV for\n50\tdisconnected installs.\n51\t\n52\t## Scope\n53\t\n54\t- Implement per-namespace PostgreSQL (pgvector) provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator\n55\t  layer for Gen AI Studio, following the model-registry-operator pattern: Deployment, Service,\n56\t  persistent storage, and a credentials Secret reconciled from the operator.\n57\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) as the provisioned\n58\t  database image; wire the image reference for disconnected installs through the existing\n59\t  `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` mechanism.\n60\t- Set the provisioned instance's resource requests/limits starting from the\n61\t  model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing.\n62\t- Implement lifecycle management via the operator's reconciliation loop: provisioning when a\n63\t  playground with RAG needs a default vector store in the namespace, and cleanup when the\n64\t  playground/namespace no longer requires it; credential rotation handled through\n65\t  reconciliation.\n66\t- Expose the provisioned instance's connection details as a namespaced reference that the\n67\t  gen-ai BFF's OGXServer wiring consumes.\n68\t- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL becomes available\n69\t  (RHOAI 3.6), the consuming wiring can switch to the shared connection string instead of the\n70\t  operator-provisioned instance.\n71\t\n72\t## Acceptance Criteria\n73\t\n74\t- The operator layer provisions a PostgreSQL 16 instance with pgvector in each namespace where\n75\t  a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG requires a default vector store, following the\n76\t  model-registry-operator provisioning pattern (Deployment, Service, persistent storage,\n77\t  credentials Secret).\n78\t- The provisioned instance uses `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` with no custom image\n79\t  build, and the image reference resolves in disconnected installs via the existing\n80\t  `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` mechanism.\n81\t- Resource requests/limits for the provisioned instance start from the model-registry\n82\t  operator's PostgreSQL sizing.\n83\t- Lifecycle is managed by reconciliation: the instance is removed when the playground or\n84\t  namespace no longer requires it, and credential rotation is supported.\n85\t- The provisioned instance's connection details are available as a namespaced reference\n86\t  consumable by the playground OGXServer wiring.\n87\t- No Konflux onboarding, repo onboarding, or custom image build is introduced by this epic.\n88\t\n89\t## HLR Traceability\n90\t\n91\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI\n92\t  without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\"\n93\t  (provisioning portion, branch A).\n94\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store runs as a separate process,\n95\t  decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider)\" (separately provisioned\n96\t  PostgreSQL instance).\n97\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for\n98\t  multi-tenant environments (e.g., per-namespace isolation)\" (per-namespace provisioning).\n99\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in\n100\t  resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead\" (reference\n101\t  resource sizing).\n102\t- Staff Engineer Input: self-provisioning via the model-registry-operator pattern in the\n103\t  operator layer from RHAISTRAT-7164; Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image with pgvector already\n104\t  exists; resource sizing referenced from model-registry-operator.\n105\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d7bb69f15af0e6e","agent_id":"a967f2b83c82d8c30","session_id":"d17e1aa1-c63c-47fc-8da1-f24a565f8f93","uuid":"3aa8532a-7545-40b9-a623-4942a2da7a7b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:43:06.303Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-94667ff5b8b7f5bd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004"}
